<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bayuda Desert</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Bayuda Desert is a rocky desert in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sudan">Sudan</a>, lying within the great bend of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nile">Nile</a> between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khartoum">Khartoum</a> and Dongola. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caravan-trade">Caravan routes</a> crossed it as a shortcut between the river's stretches. In 1885 a British column crossed it in a vain attempt to relieve Gordon at Khartoum, fighting at Abu Klea on the way.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bayuda-desert.jpg" alt="Bayuda Desert" width="320" height="219" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: NASA · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bayuda_Desert_NASA.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
